# One carried link both reader families would keep: does the judgement need it? Protocol

2026-11-10. Written before the send. A probe of a few cents inside the council round of [LOG.md](LOG.md); it changes nothing in Jev, a
prompt, a rule, the frozen judge or a saved run.

## The case

Saved D392 clean draw 3 (`stage2-clean-d3`, judged in `judged-2`). Step 1 filed four SemiAnalysis reports (Kyber delayed to 2028, the
backup plan scrapped, NVL576 affected, the four-die design cancelled) under the FY2028 total revenue question (v22), and filed
NVIDIA's answer "Our roadmap is intact" (record `70:e4`, evidence `e176`) only under the Kyber and Rubin shipping questions. A "later
version" relation carried the answer into v22. Both blind reader families would file it there as evidence; the saved judgements of
v22 cite it on 9 of 9 days it was shown.

## At no cost, done

- The untouched replay of draw 3 passes: 251 of 251 judge requests equal a saved one and took its answer; ledger, recorded requests
  and counts equal the saved run's (`poc/data/clean-step2-revision-links-2026-11-10/control-d3/`).
- With only the link `70:e4` to v22 not written (the relation kept), the days 2026-07-01 to 07-05 are identical and the first changed
  request is v22's on 2026-07-06: the `e176` block (4 lines: the statement, its quotation, and its two "Opinion, not verified" lines)
  is gone and the item count reads 8 for 9. The replay stops there (`uncarry-d3-70e4-v22/`).
- `judge_probe.py check … --case 3 v22 2026-07-06 76 e176` passes: the control is the saved request and what the code builds today;
  the two requests differ only by that block and the count; the frozen check accepts the saved answer on the control and refuses it
  on the other.

## The send

v22's request of 2026-07-06 as saved and without the carried record, three times each, interleaved, through the production
transport and the spending limit, with the sender reviewed on 2026-11-10 (`step2-edge-effect-2026-11-10/PROTOCOL.md`, "Reviews before
the send"); the only change since is that the question, day and record are arguments. Cost: $0.0585 if every send answers at once
at its reserve, $0.1755 with three attempts a send, cap $0.25; expected about $0.02.

## Reading rule, fixed now (the rule of 2026-11-10, unchanged)

Not decided unless all three answers of each arm pass the frozen check. The conclusion differs in these samples only if the three
answers without the record are on one rung and the three with it on another. No difference only if the six are on one rung.
Anything else: not decided. Read and reported beside it: the implied figure of each answer, the stated reasons, and in the arm
without the record whether the four reports are weighed with nothing set against them.

## What it can and cannot say (agreed with Codex, `council/b-codex.md`)

- It is sensitivity evidence for this one question on this one day. The previous conclusion sits at about $554 billion against a
  boundary of $550 billion, so three answers an arm may well come out mixed.
- Six answers on one rung do not show the record is not needed: both reader families would keep it, and the figure or the balance
  of the reasons may still move.
- Two rungs do not show that carrying every link is best: the direction and the reasons are read, and the 19 links the readers call
  context weigh on the other side.
- The block removed holds the record's two "Opinion, not verified" lines as well as the statement, so a difference is of the block.
- It says nothing of the four question-days that were judged only because of a carried link, nor of the days after 2026-07-06.

